tuxtoys (0.5.0~dev) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Shortcut Guide shows your own lists of shortcuts, a file per app in
    ~/.config/tuxtoys/shortcutguide/, after the app's own when it has one.
    Its settings page adds and edits them: pick one of the open windows, then
    press each shortcut's keys.
  * Find My Mouse shines a spotlight on the pointer when you press the left
    Ctrl twice, or the right one, shake the mouse, or press its shortcut,
    as PowerToys' Find My Mouse does. It watches only the pointer and the
    modifier keys, through the X RECORD extension, and takes nothing from
    other programs.
  * Mouse Highlighter shows your clicks on the screen after Super+Shift+H,
    as a ripple, a circle or a spotlight, as PowerToys' Mouse Highlighter
    does. The mouse tools share one helper process.
  * Mouse Pointer Crosshairs draws crosshairs through the pointer after
    Super+Alt+P, and its gliding cursor places the pointer and clicks with
    Super+Alt+Period alone, as PowerToys' Mouse Pointer Crosshairs does.

 -- Kōnabe Studio <konabe@proton.me>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0200

tuxtoys (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Color Picker picks a color from anywhere on the screen with
    Super+Shift+C and copies it, in sixteen formats or one of your own,
    with an editor of the last colors picked, as PowerToys' Color Picker
    does.
  * Screen Ruler measures what is on the screen with Super+Ctrl+Shift+M:
    a box dragged, or the space between the edges around the pointer, found
    as PowerToys' Screen Ruler finds them, copied with a click.
  * Text Extractor copies the text in any part of the screen with
    Super+Shift+T, read by tesseract, as it reads, on one line or as a
    table, as PowerToys' Text Extractor does. tesseract-ocr with its English
    and Hungarian data is recommended.
  * tuxtoys-settings --page opens a tool's page.
  * Shortcut Guide shows Cinnamon's keyboard shortcuts, TuxToys' and the
    active app's with Super+Shift+/, in their own words, with search and
    pins, as PowerToys' Shortcut Guide does.
  * Scrolling a settings page no longer changes the choices, numbers and
    sliders the pointer passes over.

 -- Kōnabe Studio <konabe@proton.me>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:20:00 +0200

tuxtoys (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * MintToys is now TuxToys: the package, its commands, its settings folder
    and its application ID carry the new name.
  * New+ adds New from template to Nemo's right-click menu: files and
    folders from your templates, with variables in their names and the
    templates ordered by a leading number.
  * Image Resizer resizes pictures from Nemo's right-click menu, to sizes
    of your choosing, as PowerToys' Image Resizer does.
  * Rename+ renames many files and folders at once from Nemo, with search
    and replace, regular expressions, counters, dates and a preview, as
    PowerToys' PowerRename does. It can also take over Nemo's Rename.
  * Hosts File Editor edits /etc/hosts in a window, as PowerToys' Hosts
    File Editor does, saving through pkexec with a backup first.
  * Environment Variables sets your environment variables, profiles of
    them, and the system's in /etc/environment, as PowerToys'
    Environment Variables does.
  * The settings window opens on Home, with a General page beside it: the
    version and links, the panel icon on or off, and a backup of every
    tool's settings to restore later or elsewhere.

 -- Kōnabe Studio <konabe@proton.me>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:24:15 +0200

minttoys (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Four new tools: Light Switch switches the desktop between Linux Mint's
    day and dark modes on a schedule; Always on Top keeps a window above
    the others, framed; File Locksmith shows which processes hold a file
    open; New+ manages the templates of Nemo's Create New Document.
  * A settings window with a sidebar and an Overview of every tool.
  * Awake shows its mode in the panel icon.

 -- Kōnabe Studio <konabe@proton.me>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:05:00 +0200

minttoys (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release: Awake keeps the computer awake until it is turned off,
    for a set time, or until a time of day, without changing the power
    settings. With a panel icon, a settings window and the minttoys
    command, in English and Hungarian.

 -- Kōnabe Studio <konabe@proton.me>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 13:20:00 +0200
